  {
   "section": "content.editorial-process",
   "variant": "default",
   "content": {
    "lead": "It is worth checking early assumptions against what people actually say and do. Small, regular reviews tend to surface patterns sooner than one large review at the end. Writing down the reasoning behind a decision makes it easier to revisit later. A simple checklist can keep the process consistent from one round to the next. Context matters here. Sharing progress openly invites useful questions before the work is finished. Outcomes are easier to judge when there is a baseline to compare against. Feedback from a pilot run often highlights steps that need to be clarified."
   },
